    historyContent: {
      origins: 'Pedro was developed in the United States in the nineteenth century as a variation of Pitch (All Fours). The trump 5 (Pedro) is worth five points; in Double Pedro or Cinch the other 5 of the same colour is also a trump. The game was extremely widely played in the US at the end of the nineteenth century and declined in the twentieth; it remains popular in the southern USA, West Coast, Louisiana, Nicaragua, and in Finland as Pidro.',
